From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:19:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: GLM tool calls streamed whole in their place, calls
 at the end of the think block, agent histories that render, TF_GLM_TOOL_CALLS
 (MiaAI-Lab recipe patches 0036, 0051, 0056)

MiaAI-Lab's recipe (github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold @ 1576746) serves GLM-5.3-Flash
to agent clients with tool-call fixes that TensorFold 0.6.5 lacks. This ports, behind TF_GLM_TOOL_CALLS=1 (off
unless set; the recipe has no switch for them), the end state of recipe patches 0036-glm-tool-calls (with 0053's and
0055's changes to its streamer), 0051-glm-tool-history-recovery and the text part of 0056-glm-tool-result-media
(Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab; parts of 0036 adapted from jayleaton/glm53-tensorfold-spark patch
0620, Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 Jay Leaton), and 0036's kept reasoning behind its own TF_GLM_KEEP_REASONING
(default 0 here, 1024 in the recipe):

- cuda/reply_text.py: GlmCallStreamer follows each GLM call while it is written and sends it whole, header and
  arguments in one delta, in its place in the stream once its </tool_call> arrives (0.6.5 sends GLM's calls after
  the reply ends, and nothing while a long call such as a file write is written). ThinkSplit: calls written inside
  the think block are the reply's calls when they end it, else reasoning (0.6.5 reads a call in an unclosed block as
  the answer, text after it included). Both copied from the recipe's end state.
- cuda/server.py App.run: the streamer for GLM's streamed replies (other families keep ToolCallStreamer), an empty
  delta every CALL_KEEPALIVE_S (2 s) while a call is held, a call the reply ends inside (its token limit, a stop
  string) never sent nor its markup as content, finish "length"/"stop" for such a reply; #285's closing of a call
  the end token left open is unchanged. cuda/http.py sends the calls the reply's end closed.
- families/glm5_next/prompts.py agent_history (the CUDA and Mac servers): a call's arguments sent as "" or null are
  no arguments (0.6.5 renders them as an _invalid_arguments argument the model never wrote); a call whose
  arguments are not a JSON object is left out with its result and logged (0051; 0.6.5 renders it under
  _invalid_arguments); results whose ids match none of their calls' render in the order sent (the checkpoint's
  template drops them). server/messages.py: a step's `reasoning` field is its reasoning_content.
- App._prepare + server/prompts.py tool_media_parts: without --vision, a GLM tool result's pictures render as the
  checkpoint template's own "unable to process this image" reminder instead of HTTP 400 on every later turn of the
  agent session (0056's text part; its image path needs GLM vision, which this tree does not have).
- tool_parameters.py (every parser and both streamers, as in the recipe): a parameter schema's type list, anyOf /
  oneOf, enum or const types its value, and a nullable string's null is None; engine/tool_draft.py streams it.
- families/glm5_next/cuda/kept_reasoning.py (new) + GlmApp: a tool-calling reply's reasoning is kept and put back
  into a later request whose client dropped it, found by the server's call ids or a signature of the whole
  conversation before the calls (TF_GLM_KEEP_REASONING replies, TF_GLM_KEEP_REASONING_MB of text).

Unset, every path is TensorFold 0.6.5's (+ #285): the shared decoder reads a single type name only, and the server's
replies and prompts are byte-identical.

Tests: tests/test_glm_tool_fixes.py (CPU, through GlmApp and the HTTP handler: streamed calls in their place, drafted
rounds, keepalive deltas, cut calls, think-block calls, tool_choice none / named / required / auto,
parallel_tool_calls false, func_probe's exact case, empty and malformed arguments and null content in the history,
renumbered result ids, the reasoning field, a tool result's picture without --vision, kept reasoning, schema types;
with the checkpoint's own template when TF_GLM5_TR3_MODEL points at it; with smooth streaming once
tensorfold.cuda.stream_pacing is in the tree). tests/test_glm_tool_call_end.py: #285's two cut-call cases read the
switch (with it, the cut markup is not content).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM tool calls") and the ported units' docstrings name MiaAI-Lab, the patches and
Jay Leaton's project.

